# .zdots.local — Machine-local identity and overrides
#
# This file is sourced AFTER .zdots.env and .zdots.secrets.
# It is gitignored and never committed. Copy this file to .zdots.local
# and fill in values for this specific machine.
#
#   cp .zdots.local.example .zdots.local
#
# Values set here override anything from .zdots.env.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine context — REQUIRED on every machine.
# Options: home | work
# work: enforces ZDOTS_AI_MODE=local, ZDOTS_CAPTURE_ENABLED=0,
#       ZDOTS_HISTORY_REDACT=1, and triggers SIP/FileVault checks in
#       zdots-ctl check. Do not leave as 'home' on a regulated machine.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ZDOTS_CONTEXT=home

# compinit: silence the group-writable prompt for /opt/homebrew/share.
# Homebrew sets g+w intentionally; compaudit flags it on every compdump rebuild
# (post-brew-update, post new completion file). bin/check already treats this
# path as a known system-managed path. The -i flag silently ignores it.
# ZDOTS_COMPLETION_PERMISSIVE=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
# Default ZDOTS_MIGRATION_URL uses peer auth as the OS user (postgresql:///my).
# This works on macOS/Homebrew where the installing user is a PG superuser.
# Override here if your setup differs (e.g., different PG port, named user).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ZDOTS_MIGRATION_URL=postgresql:///my
# ZDOTS_POSTGRES_VERSION=17               # Set if using PostgreSQL 17 (default: 18)
# ZDOTS_SKIP_POSTGRES_BREW=1             # Set to 1 if Postgres is already installed and managed externally
# brew bundle only sees HOMEBREW_-prefixed variables (Homebrew scrubs the rest
# of the environment), so the Brewfile needs the prefixed, exported form too:
# export HOMEBREW_ZDOTS_POSTGRES_VERSION=17 HOMEBREW_ZDOTS_SKIP_POSTGRES_BREW=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI security boundary (NON-NEGOTIABLE on a new machine)
#
# local  — ZDOTS_AI_ENDPOINT only. No cloud API keys. Safe default.
# cloud  — Enables cloud APIs. Keys MUST live in .zdots.secrets, not here.
#
# Do NOT change this to "cloud" until:
#   1. Security review is complete for this machine
#   2. Cloud API keys are stored in .zdots.secrets (gitignored)
#   3. You understand what data will leave this machine
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ZDOTS_AI_MODE=local

# AI endpoints — local defaults or a trusted LAN machine.
# ZDOTS_AI_ENDPOINT:       chat/completions (port 11500, Qwen3-8B)
# ZDOTS_AI_EMBED_ENDPOINT: embeddings only  (port 11501, Nomic embed-v2 MoE)
# Both are used by zdots-ctx, zdots-brain, and ai-query.
#
# Override for a remote inference machine:
#   ZDOTS_AI_ENDPOINT=http://powerstation.local:11500
#   ZDOTS_AI_EMBED_ENDPOINT=http://powerstation.local:11501
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ZDOTS_AI_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:11500
# ZDOTS_AI_EMBED_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:11501
# ZDOTS_AI_PROFILE=qwen3-8b

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Colima VM sizing & hardware tuning (M5 / 24GB+ machines)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ZDOTS_COLIMA_CPU=6                      # Default: 4
# ZDOTS_COLIMA_MEMORY=10                  # Default: 8 (GiB) — 10-12 on 24GB hosts
# ZDOTS_COLIMA_DISK=100                   # Default: 60 (GiB) — 100-150 on 1TB hosts
# ZDOTS_COLIMA_KUBERNETES=1               # Default: 1 (k3s bundled alongside Docker)
# ZDOTS_SPEC_DECODING=1                   # Enable speculative decoding (supported on 24GB)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PHI safety controls (relevant when ZDOTS_CONTEXT=work or near regulated data)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Database encryption key — required before enabling session capture.
# Store the key in macOS Keychain (never hardcode it here):
#   security add-generic-password \
#     -a "$USER" -s "ZDOTS_DB_ENCRYPTION_KEY" \
#     -w "$(openssl rand -hex 32)" -T "" ~/Library/Keychains/login.keychain-db
# Then uncomment the line below to load it at shell startup:
# export ZDOTS_DB_ENCRYPTION_KEY=$(zdots-keychain get ZDOTS_DB_ENCRYPTION_KEY 2>/dev/null)

# Session capture — disabled by default. Requires:
#   1. ZDOTS_DB_ENCRYPTION_KEY set above (Keychain-backed)
#   2. Embedding server running on ZDOTS_AI_EMBED_ENDPOINT (:11501)
#   3. zdots-ctx migrate run to apply the latest schema
#   4. ZDOTS_CONTEXT=home (capture is always off on work machines)
# ZDOTS_CAPTURE_ENABLED=1

# History redaction — on by default (1). Set to 0 to disable (not recommended
# on machines that may handle PHI).
# ZDOTS_HISTORY_REDACT=1

# Command analytics — captures every executed command to SQLite with exit code,
# duration, CWD, and session ID (conf.d/56-cmd-analytics.zsh). Syncs to the
# PostgreSQL command_runs table via `zdots-ctx sync-history` (auto-runs on capture).
# Prerequisite: zdots-ctx migrate (adds command_runs + sync_state tables).
# Credential patterns in args are redacted inline before write.
# Disabled unconditionally on work machines (.zdots.work enforces CMD_ANALYTICS=0).
# ZDOTS_CMD_ANALYTICS=1

# Site-specific redaction patterns belong in etc/phi-patterns.yaml (committed
# to git — it is configuration, not a secret). The PHI Pattern Registry is the
# sole source of truth: patterns defined there apply automatically to the
# history hook, analytics capture, and AI pipeline with no per-layer wiring.
# See the POSIX ERE + YAML format already used in that file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Speaker diarization (transcription pipeline — opt-in, home context)
# Enables the ingest_media "diarized" stage: pyannote acoustic speaker turns
# over each transcript. Off by default.
# Requires HUGGINGFACE_TOKEN in Keychain (read-only) — see .zdots.secrets.example
# for how to register the token and accept the gated pyannote model licenses.
# The worker loads that token from Keychain at runtime; nothing secret goes here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ZDOTS_DIARIZE=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# yt-dlp cookies (Z-237) — bot-gated fetches (recipes/yt-transcribe,
# bin/zdots-ingest-media). YouTube rejects some anonymous fetches with
# "Sign in to confirm you're not a bot" or a bare HTTP 403 on the media URL.
# Default is no cookies (fine for non-gated sources: Vimeo, archive.org).
# File wins if both are set. See lib/ytdlp.bash for the two knobs.
# Cookies are passed to yt-dlp only — never written to DB, analytics, or logs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ZDOTS_YTDLP_COOKIES_FROM_BROWSER=chrome   # firefox|chrome|safari|brave|edge[:profile]
# ZDOTS_YTDLP_COOKIES_FILE=/path/to/cookies.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Work context overrides (only relevant when ZDOTS_CONTEXT=work)
# Keep corporate identity and network config here, not in the shared repo.
# Git identity: do not export GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL / GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL here — they
# override the includeIf scoping that keeps platform repos on the personal
# identity. Put the work address in ~/.config/git/config.identity instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HTTP_PROXY=http://corporate-proxy:8080
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://corporate-proxy:8080
# NO_PROXY=localhost,127.0.0.1,.internal,.corp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Managed (MDM) Macs — let the employer baseline win where it already covers a
# need. See docs/work-migration-playbook.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ZDOTS_GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=0     # employer manages ~/.gitconfig (identity, signing): read it too
# ZDOTS_WORK_RELATIVE_PATH=0    # no ./bin, ./node_modules/.bin, … entries on PATH
# ZDOTS_LOCAL_BIN=0             # no cd hook prepending $PWD/bin
# export HOMEBREW_ZDOTS_SKIP_1PASSWORD_INSTALL=1   # MDM installs 1Password and its CLI
# export HOMEBREW_ZDOTS_SKIP_CHROME_INSTALL=1      # MDM installs Chrome

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Work-extension layer (Z-262, AGENTS.md §10) — the ONLY sanctioned place a
# tenant/employer's own identity, PHI patterns, and app wiring enter the
# platform. Everything else stays employer-agnostic and tracked here.
#
# ZDOTS_WORK_EXT points at a SEPARATE repo (own history, own remote, never
# a submodule) that conf.d/31-work-ext.zsh sources if present:
#   $ZDOTS_WORK_EXT/init.zsh              — sourced at shell startup
#   $ZDOTS_WORK_EXT/phi-patterns.d/*.yaml — PHI pattern overlay (merged by
#                                            zdots-otel-phi-compile; can only
#                                            ADD patterns/exemptions, never
#                                            edit or remove a base rule)
#   $ZDOTS_WORK_EXT/otel.d/*.yaml         — cors_origins / app_service_name
#                                            overlay for etc/otel-collector.yaml
# Absent dir = personal machine = every line below is a silent no-op.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ZDOTS_WORK_EXT=~/.config/zdots-work
# ZDOTS_K8S_DEFAULT_NS=
# ZDOTS_APP_LOG=
